### MEDIUM: gemini (gemini-code-assist[bot])
**File**: `.agents/scripts/simplex-bot/src/commands.ts:116`
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `tasksCommand` handler suppresses `grep` errors with `2>/dev/null`, which can hide issues like file permission errors. A more robust approach is to handle `grep`'s exit codes explicitly. `grep` exits with 0 for matches, 1 for no matches, and >1 for errors.

```typescript
  handler: async (_ctx: CommandContext): Promise<string> => {
    try {
      const proc = Bun.spawn(["grep", "-c", "\\- \[ \]", "TODO.md"], {
        stdout: "pipe",
        stderr: "pipe",
      });

      const exitCode = await proc.exited;

      if (exitCode === 0) {
        const count = (await new Response(proc.stdout).text()).trim();
        return `Open tasks: ${count}\n\nUse /task <description> to create a new task.`;
      } else if (exitCode === 1) {
        // grep returns 1 when no lines are selected, which is not an error here.
        return "Open tasks: 0\n\nUse /task <description> to create a new task.";
      } else {
        // grep returns > 1 for errors like file not found.
        const error = await new Response(proc.stderr).text();
        if (error.includes("No such file or directory")) {
          return "Open tasks: 0\n\nUse /task <description> to create a new task.";
        }
        console.error(`[tasksCommand] grep failed: ${error}`);
        return "Could not read TODO.md";
      }
    } catch (e) {
      console.error(`[tasksCommand] Error: ${e}`);
      return "Could not read TODO.md";
    }
  },
```

