### MEDIUM: gemini (gemini-code-assist[bot])
**File**: `scripts/npm-postinstall.cjs:76`
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `fs.closeSync(ttyFd)` call is not wrapped in a `try...catch` block. If closing the file descriptor fails for any reason, it will throw an unhandled exception and terminate the script. While the `postinstall` command in `package.json` uses `|| true` to prevent installation failure, making the script itself more robust is a good practice.

I recommend wrapping the `closeSync` call in a `try...catch` block to handle potential errors gracefully during cleanup.

```
if (ttyFd !== null) {
    try {
        fs.closeSync(ttyFd);
    } catch {
        // Ignore errors on close, as there's nothing more to do.
    }
}
```

